(398053, 33367, 8911, '<td valign="top">This is a really cool use of negative space. It''s weakened by several factors, though: the near rocks are straight, but the horizon and even the ground by the boy (to the left) are at an angle; focus could be crisper (I''m not sure what it focussed on); and the light behind the boy glares so much that his hand appears to be patchwork lace. It''s a lovely setup, and I suspect a few more angles and different exposure times would have produced a crisper show of what you were trying to do with this one.</td>', 'This is a really cool use of negative space. It''s weakened by several factors, though: the near rocks are straight, but the horizon and even the ground by the boy (to the left) are at an angle; focus could be crisper (I''m not sure what it focussed on); and the light behind the boy glares so much that his hand appears to be patchwork lace. It''s a lovely setup, and I suspect a few more angles and different exposure times would have produced a crisper show of what you were trying to do with this one.', '2003-08-24 21:55:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(398057, 33587, 6521, '<td valign="top">simple but classy</td>', 'simple but classy', '2003-08-24 21:56:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(398067, 33264, 8911, '<td valign="top">That''s a pretty skyline, though a bit blurred by the distance. I''m not sure you don''t have too much negative space here, though - it sort of overwhlems the photograph. If I scroll until it looks roughly square, it seems a bit stronger as an image.</td>', 'That''s a pretty skyline, though a bit blurred by the distance. I''m not sure you don''t have too much negative space here, though - it sort of overwhlems the photograph. If I scroll until it looks roughly square, it seems a bit stronger as an image.', '2003-08-24 22:01:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(398069, 34012, 8911, '<td valign="top">This is good for a grin, besides being a decent photo. It might have been worth a few more tries, though - the one on the right is holding his head higher than the one on the left, so that the lines are wrong for the vase (and the noises/mouths/eyes are not directly across from each other).</td>', 'This is good for a grin, besides being a decent photo. It might have been worth a few more tries, though - the one on the right is holding his head higher than the one on the left, so that the lines are wrong for the vase (and the noises/mouths/eyes are not directly across from each other).', '2003-08-24 22:02:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(398071, 33629, 8911, '<td valign="top">How''d you get him to cooperate so well? This is a nice image, though it''s a pity that most of the ''hopper is out of focus - it''s visually distracting and hard to say whether that''s a positive or a negative space.</td>', 'How''d you get him to cooperate so well? This is a nice image, though it''s a pity that most of the ''hopper is out of focus - it''s visually distracting and hard to say whether that''s a positive or a negative space.', '2003-08-24 22:04:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(398074, 33756, 8911, '<td valign="top">Hee. I love this guy - he''s great. (And suitably grumpy-looking!) I don''t know that the negative space really creates the "wow!", though. It seems more just to be there - I felt the image looked stronger when moved so that the toad more of the frame.</td>', 'Hee. I love this guy - he''s great. (And suitably grumpy-looking!) I don''t know that the negative space really creates the "wow!", though. It seems more just to be there - I felt the image looked stronger when moved so that the toad more of the frame.', '2003-08-24 22:06:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(398077, 33175, 8911, '<td valign="top">This is really beautiful, and really fascinating. It''s also very, very visually "busy" - I''m really not sure where the negative space is supposed to be in this. If it were just the black-and-white pattern, I''d take the white for negative space, but whatever the layer is over it adding distortion, it seems to disturb the flow of my eyes over the photo enough to keep from really settling on that.</td>', 'This is really beautiful, and really fascinating. It''s also very, very visually "busy" - I''m really not sure where the negative space is supposed to be in this. If it were just the black-and-white pattern, I''d take the white for negative space, but whatever the layer is over it adding distortion, it seems to disturb the flow of my eyes over the photo enough to keep from really settling on that.', '2003-08-24 22:08:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(398086, 33820, 2983, '<td valign="top">A bit off center, off balance, but very artistic image.</td>', 'A bit off center, off balance, but very artistic image.', '2003-08-24 22:21:58.000000', NULL, 1),
