(398106, 33628, 9232, '<td valign="top">It seems like the "pop" of this image isn''t dependant on the negative space but rather on the inverted eye within the drop.  Perhaps that''s just the first thing I focus on but each time I''ve been through the images it just seems to be the focal point.  I like the technique, the lighting you chose and the background image.  It just seems to be a study in refractive composition (pun intended) rather than negative space. - 5</td>', 'It seems like the "pop" of this image isn''t dependant on the negative space but rather on the inverted eye within the drop.  Perhaps that''s just the first thing I focus on but each time I''ve been through the images it just seems to be the focal point.  I like the technique, the lighting you chose and the background image.  It just seems to be a study in refractive composition (pun intended) rather than negative space. - 5', '2003-08-24 22:35:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(398107, 33448, 5705, '<td valign="top">Super Capture-- WOW -- 10</td>', 'Super Capture-- WOW -- 10', '2003-08-24 22:35:52.000000', NULL, 1),
