(398510, 33431, 3320, '<td valign="top">Loved that picture and guessed it was you (without being able to put a name on it). Nice ''oldish'' tones and I usually do not like backgrounds that shows if they are black, white or purple) but this one does serve the mood and gives to me the sensation of not a ''portrait in the present'' but a ''reproductio nof a model posing for a photographer long time ago''. Do not know if it is was was neant .. but I like it. Very good job. Lionel</td>', 'Loved that picture and guessed it was you (without being able to put a name on it). Nice ''oldish'' tones and I usually do not like backgrounds that shows if they are black, white or purple) but this one does serve the mood and gives to me the sensation of not a ''portrait in the present'' but a ''reproductio nof a model posing for a photographer long time ago''. Do not know if it is was was neant .. but I like it. Very good job. Lionel', '2003-08-25 08:47:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(398516, 33760, 2780, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the ribbon :)</td>', 'Congrats on the ribbon :)', '2003-08-25 08:53:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(398525, 33431, 200, '<td valign="top">I purposely lightened the background to create a sense of texture and that of an old painting. It also brought out more detail in the various shadows. My monitor is darker than most I suppose. I tried to reach a happy medium..knowing others are going to see this lighter than some. If I could print the image...then everyone could know exactly how this was meant to look. The background is black...and seemed a bit too cliche to leave simply black...i was playing with light and playing in general. I never expected this image to do as well as it did. I was figuring in the low 5''s at best. BUT...I really liked the image...so submitted it anyway :)</td>', 'I purposely lightened the background to create a sense of texture and that of an old painting. It also brought out more detail in the various shadows. My monitor is darker than most I suppose. I tried to reach a happy medium..knowing others are going to see this lighter than some. If I could print the image...then everyone could know exactly how this was meant to look. The background is black...and seemed a bit too cliche to leave simply black...i was playing with light and playing in general. I never expected this image to do as well as it did. I was figuring in the low 5''s at best. BUT...I really liked the image...so submitted it anyway :)', '2003-08-25 09:00:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(398543, 33629, 2716, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the nice comments.<br/> <br/>Thanks Mag.  This is my fourth Purple Ribbon (5th place); it will go nice with my five Green Ribbons (4th place).  lol.<br/></td>', 'Thanks for the nice comments. Thanks Mag.  This is my fourth Purple Ribbon (5th place); it will go nice with my five Green Ribbons (4th place).  lol.', '2003-08-25 09:32:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(398545, 33047, 9411, '<td valign="top">Thank you all for making this my best finish to date!<br/> <br/>Many have asked how I did this shot. <br/> <br/>Well, it was actually very simple. The only thing that might be difficult for most is having a sheet of dicrhoic glass on hand to use as a background. Black glass that has a ripple texture makes the base. <br/> <br/>This was lit with ceiling bounced EiKO Photoflood &amp; an angled diffused side light. <br/> <br/>The only Photoshop tool used was the unsharp Mask. <br/> <br/>I sure do appreciate all the helpful comments.</td>', 'Thank you all for making this my best finish to date! Many have asked how I did this shot.  Well, it was actually very simple. The only thing that might be difficult for most is having a sheet of dicrhoic glass on hand to use as a background. Black glass that has a ripple texture makes the base.  This was lit with ceiling bounced EiKO Photoflood & an angled diffused side light.  The only Photoshop tool used was the unsharp Mask.  I sure do appreciate all the helpful comments.', '2003-08-25 09:33:26.000000', NULL, 0),
