(404611, 33729, 811, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUE<br/>by karmat<br/> <br/>Overall, I think this is a good picture, and that you have used negative space to emphasize your subject.  I do feel the framing/cropping is a bit tight, and as a result, feels off balanced.  More space on either side, and more on top would have really made the NS seem dramatic, I think.  The exposure seems to work well, as the colors are vivid without being blown out, and the focus seems okay.  The details of the window are crystal clear, but I suspect that is a distance thing rather than a focus thing.  The only thing that really bothers me about this shot is that even though it is straight (as can be evidenced by the bottom of the center window), it stills feels loopy to me.  Some of it is probably distortion caused by shots like this, but it just feels like you need to move a few inches to your right when this was shot.  I saw the comment about existing artwork, and though I many not agree with it, it may have been interesting to put someone or something in front of the window to create a silhouette.  Someone praying or something.  Of course, I don''t know the logistics, but if it had been possible, it would have added a definite focal point to the shot.<br/> <br/>Best to you in future challenges<br/>karmat</td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUEby karmat Overall, I think this is a good picture, and that you have used negative space to emphasize your subject.  I do feel the framing/cropping is a bit tight, and as a result, feels off balanced.  More space on either side, and more on top would have really made the NS seem dramatic, I think.  The exposure seems to work well, as the colors are vivid without being blown out, and the focus seems okay.  The details of the window are crystal clear, but I suspect that is a distance thing rather than a focus thing.  The only thing that really bothers me about this shot is that even though it is straight (as can be evidenced by the bottom of the center window), it stills feels loopy to me.  Some of it is probably distortion caused by shots like this, but it just feels like you need to move a few inches to your right when this was shot.  I saw the comment about existing artwork, and though I many not agree with it, it may have been interesting to put someone or something in front of the window to create a silhouette.  Someone praying or something.  Of course, I don''t know the logistics, but if it had been possible, it would have added a definite focal point to the shot. Best to you in future challengeskarmat', '2003-08-30 12:03:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(404635, 33448, 714, '<td valign="top">Another beautiful image. congrats!</td>', 'Another beautiful image. congrats!', '2003-08-30 13:04:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(404733, 33457, 6202, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>This definately does fit the challenge.  There is a lot of negative space here.<br/> <br/>The darkness of the building works nicely against the blue sky.  The sky works well as it appears to be a very clear day.  I know you used ruled of thirds in your composition but in this case I think if you had centered the point of the roof and kept it to the bottom third it might work very well.  As it is I feel like we are missing part of the artifacts on the building.<br/> <br/>Anna</td>', '*Critique Club* This definately does fit the challenge.  There is a lot of negative space here. The darkness of the building works nicely against the blue sky.  The sky works well as it appears to be a very clear day.  I know you used ruled of thirds in your composition but in this case I think if you had centered the point of the roof and kept it to the bottom third it might work very well.  As it is I feel like we are missing part of the artifacts on the building. Anna', '2003-08-30 16:25:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(404735, 33369, 6202, '<td valign="top">Critique Club<br/> <br/>Definately fits the challenge of Negative Space.  There is a good bit of detail to the feather, the lighting appears to be pretty good.  Your composition is also good.<br/> <br/>The only thing this really lacks is the luster to win.  As it is right now it reminds me of Forrest Gump without the box of chocolates.  In other words it is just a little to plain to win.<br/> <br/>Anna</td>', 'Critique Club Definately fits the challenge of Negative Space.  There is a good bit of detail to the feather, the lighting appears to be pretty good.  Your composition is also good. The only thing this really lacks is the luster to win.  As it is right now it reminds me of Forrest Gump without the box of chocolates.  In other words it is just a little to plain to win. Anna', '2003-08-30 16:28:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(404737, 33586, 6202, '<td valign="top">Critique Club<br/> <br/>Good shot!  Excellent entry for this challenge.  I personally envy you for being able to take this fantastic photo.  <br/> <br/>Only thing that might have improved it was a deeper saturation of color there was a grayish tone to it overall and making the black a deeper bolder black would have brought out the planet more.<br/> <br/>Anna</td>', 'Critique Club Good shot!  Excellent entry for this challenge.  I personally envy you for being able to take this fantastic photo.   Only thing that might have improved it was a deeper saturation of color there was a grayish tone to it overall and making the black a deeper bolder black would have brought out the planet more. Anna', '2003-08-30 16:36:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(404738, 33548, 6202, '<td valign="top">Critique Club<br/> <br/>The colors here are real attention grabbers.  The photo itself seems to be evenly divided into thirds and has a very special beauty all its own.<br/> <br/>Very good work and I hope to see more photos like this from you in future.  <br/> <br/>Anna</td>', 'Critique Club The colors here are real attention grabbers.  The photo itself seems to be evenly divided into thirds and has a very special beauty all its own. Very good work and I hope to see more photos like this from you in future.   Anna', '2003-08-30 16:38:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(404761, 33907, 5728, '<td valign="top">Critique Club once again<br/> <br/>Greetings to Iceland. You''ve met the challenge with this photo, lots of negative space around your main subject. I gave you a 7 for this pic because I like the yellow/blue combination.<br/> <br/>What kind of hit me on the negative side about your image is that you centered the 13. It is exactly in the middle and I would have prefered to have seen it in one of the corners. You know, rule of thirds etc. I also think the border is a little overwhelming and pulls me away from your pic too much.<br/> <br/>You certainly didn''t deserve the 1''s, 2''s and 3''s you got here.<br/> <br/>See ya<br/> <br/>Gary</td>', 'Critique Club once again Greetings to Iceland. You''ve met the challenge with this photo, lots of negative space around your main subject. I gave you a 7 for this pic because I like the yellow/blue combination. What kind of hit me on the negative side about your image is that you centered the 13. It is exactly in the middle and I would have prefered to have seen it in one of the corners. You know, rule of thirds etc. I also think the border is a little overwhelming and pulls me away from your pic too much. You certainly didn''t deserve the 1''s, 2''s and 3''s you got here. See ya Gary', '2003-08-30 17:40:57.000000', NULL, 0),
