(3814260, 34026, 32997, '<td valign="top">you know, this is one beautifully rendered shot...somehow so alive and quite unique!</td>', 'you know, this is one beautifully rendered shot...somehow so alive and quite unique!', '2007-06-21 09:56:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(3930312, 33431, 66635, '<td valign="top">Wow!  Magnificent.</td>', 'Wow!  Magnificent.', '2007-07-23 23:13:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(4555982, 33777, 59029, '<td valign="top">Excellent use of thirds and negative space IMHO.  And if you do want to learn your camera in a hurry, then definitely do what you did here...shoot, and shoot a lot, until you get what you want.<br/> <br/>Other useful stuff for backdrops: bristol board is dirt cheap, comes in large sheets and can be rolled up when not in use.  I''ve also used a black towel draped over a doorway for a terrific, non-reflective bg.  You''re doing well, keep shooting!</td>', 'Excellent use of thirds and negative space IMHO.  And if you do want to learn your camera in a hurry, then definitely do what you did here...shoot, and shoot a lot, until you get what you want. Other useful stuff for backdrops: bristol board is dirt cheap, comes in large sheets and can be rolled up when not in use.  I''ve also used a black towel draped over a doorway for a terrific, non-reflective bg.  You''re doing well, keep shooting!', '2008-03-11 20:10:49.000000', NULL, 0),
